{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01684",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 6.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Hi, uh, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.08,
      "end_seconds": 13.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 18.13,
      "end_seconds": 23.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.7,
      "end_seconds": 28.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I'm here because of a very fast heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.13,
      "end_seconds": 35.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.31,
      "end_seconds": 41.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "About about a month, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 42.44,
      "end_seconds": 48.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "I, I think it's been nearer about two months, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.75,
      "end_seconds": 53.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.59,
      "end_seconds": 56.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.72,
      "end_seconds": 66.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.11,
      "end_seconds": 79.06,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Honestly, a couple of times a week. Mild, really. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.62,
      "end_seconds": 87.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "And, And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 87.8,
      "end_seconds": 93.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.42,
      "end_seconds": 101.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.03,
      "end_seconds": 107.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.35,
      "end_seconds": 112.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "So, and I've been feeling faint as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 114.14,
      "end_seconds": 120.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Blood pressure 103 over 64, saturation 96 percent, heart rate 99."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.58,
      "end_seconds": 123.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.17,
      "end_seconds": 126.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.34,
      "end_seconds": 128.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.29,
      "end_seconds": 148.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Your pulse is over one hundred and eighty and your blood pressure is low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.1,
      "end_seconds": 158.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Alright, a few quick ones: leg swelling, fever or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.44,
      "end_seconds": 173.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "So, no, no leg swelling, no fever, no cough. I was sweating at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.73,
      "end_seconds": 175.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.56,
      "end_seconds": 179.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.36,
      "end_seconds": 185.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.83,
      "end_seconds": 198.57,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "I, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.4,
      "end_seconds": 213.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.84,
      "end_seconds": 219.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.76,
      "end_seconds": 223.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.27,
      "end_seconds": 229.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.85,
      "end_seconds": 234.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.33,
      "end_seconds": 241.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Okay, so my daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.28,
      "end_seconds": 245.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.35,
      "end_seconds": 255.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Let me think, I've had heart disease for five years now. Yes, arthritis in my knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.34,
      "end_seconds": 257.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Yes, carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.61,
      "end_seconds": 259.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.45,
      "end_seconds": 265.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "So, which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.63,
      "end_seconds": 275.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "Actually, I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. I'm on paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.61,
      "end_seconds": 279.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.59,
      "end_seconds": 285.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "650 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.59,
      "end_seconds": 294.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Actually, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.52,
      "end_seconds": 299.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.78,
      "end_seconds": 311.97,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "Ah, for my sugar, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.93,
      "end_seconds": 342.04,
      "duration_seconds": 22.11,
      "text": "Putting it all together, this looks most like a dangerous fast heart rhythm. Supraventricular tachycardia is also on my list. I'm sending you for blood tests because of arrhythmia. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. An urgent ECG is what I'd like next, for fast heart rhythm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.65,
      "end_seconds": 346.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.03,
      "end_seconds": 356.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "Lie flat, I am calling the emergency team and preparing to shock the heart. We'll refer you to the emergency team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.68,
      "end_seconds": 362.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Well, um, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.05,
      "end_seconds": 371.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Book a review straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.0,
      "end_seconds": 373.7,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.66,
      "end_seconds": 380.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.43,
      "end_seconds": 386.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}